@startuml Command

title Command Pattern — Telegram Bot Command Dispatch

skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
skinparam classFontStyle bold

' ── Command interface ──────────────────────────────────────────
interface ICommand <<interface>> {
  + ExecuteAsync(message : Message, user : User) : Task
}

' ── Abstract base command ──────────────────────────────────────
abstract class AdminOnlyCommand <<abstract>> {
  - _botClient : ITelegramBotClient
  - _adminTelegramIds : long[]
  + ExecuteAsync(message : Message, user : User) : Task
  # {abstract} ExecuteAdminAsync(message : Message, user : User) : Task
}

' ── Concrete Commands ──────────────────────────────────────────
class StartCommand {
  + ExecuteAsync(...) : Task
}

class HelpCommand {
  + ExecuteAsync(...) : Task
}

class FormatsCommand {
  + ExecuteAsync(...) : Task
}

class TestUploadCommand {
  # ExecuteAdminAsync(...) : Task
}

' Note: SingleAudioUploadCommand has moved to a session-based 
' processing model, but still implements ICommand for consistency.
class SingleAudioUploadCommand {
  + ResumeSessionAsync(memento : UploadSessionMemento) : Task
}

' ── Invoker & Router ───────────────────────────────────────────
class CommandRouter {
  - _catalog : ICommandCatalog
  + RouteMessageAsync(message : Message) : Task
}

class UpdateHandler {
  - _commandRouter : CommandRouter
  - _uploadQueue : IUploadSessionQueue
  + HandleUpdateAsync(...) : Task
}

' ── Relationships ──────────────────────────────────────────────
AdminOnlyCommand ..|> ICommand
StartCommand ..|> ICommand
HelpCommand ..|> ICommand
FormatsCommand ..|> ICommand
TestUploadCommand --|> AdminOnlyCommand
SingleAudioUploadCommand ..|> ICommand

UpdateHandler --> CommandRouter : "routes text commands"
UpdateHandler --> IUploadSessionQueue : "enqueues file uploads"
CommandRouter ..> ICommand : "invokes"

note bottom of UpdateHandler
  **Dispatcher**
  Differentiates between text 
  commands (Command Pattern) 
  and file uploads (Iterator/Memento 
  Pipeline).
end note

footer Command Pattern · NurFlac
@enduml
